WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:02.776
- Say hello to Dulé.

00:00:02.776 --> 00:00:03.609
- Oh yeah.

00:00:03.609 --> 00:00:04.442
- Yeah, we did.

00:00:04.442 --> 00:00:05.330
- Did you watch The West Wing?
Were you a West Wing fan?

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.660
- Uh, I did not.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.277
Actually I grew up without television.

00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:09.110
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.584
- I grew up in the Bush in Australia, so,

00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:12.810
I didn't have television
until I was 12 years old.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.650
So it's not the thing for me to watch TV

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.620
- [Kelly] Gravitate towards, yeah.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.030
- Yeah, it's kinda weird.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:19.890
But I've seen your work. It's amazing.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.240
- It's not weird, it's just different.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.850
That's cool, what did you do?

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:23.683
- Nothing.

00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.090
- Nothing? Yeah, it's like,
did you - obviously music?

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.750
- Yeah. We used to sit around
the piano and sing songs.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.590
- Maybe that's why you're
so incredibly gifted.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.860
Cuz you were like, nah,
I'm gonna invest in myself,

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.329
my talent, and my work
right in front of me.

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:36.210
- Well, it's just, it wasn't the thing.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.520
You know, I just started to learn piano

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.350
and my dad was in the Army,
but he was a singer as well.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.040
And so after dinner we'd
sit around the piano,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.700
and we had a player
piano, which I have now.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.420
After my mom died, I got it.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.440
And we'd, you know, pump the little pedals

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.273
and we'd sing along.

00:00:51.273 --> 00:00:54.140
It was all the show tunes, it
was pretty amazing actually.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.360
- I love that.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.590
Was there a real Jessie?

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.423
I know everybody's had to ask you this

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:58.580
but I don't know this.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.470
Was there a real Jessie?
Like was there a girlfriend?

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.044
Was this a real story?

00:01:04.044 --> 00:01:05.019
- No, I just made it up.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:05.956
- [Kelly] No!

00:01:05.956 --> 00:01:07.152
(Dulé laughs)

00:01:07.152 --> 00:01:08.140
- No, I just made up.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:08.973
No, it was a real story.

00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:11.040
It was, I hadn't written for a while

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.330
and I was thinking maybe the music thing-

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.690
I'd been an actor for a while

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.820
but it wasn't really making
a lot of money back then.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.742
I thought, maybe I better
look for something else

00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:20.910
to support my future family.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.315
So I thought that I'd become
a stained glass master.

00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:25.750
- (gasps) Do you know how to do that?

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.350
- Which is sounding like
a great choice, right,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.842
if you wanna support your family.

00:01:28.842 --> 00:01:30.324
- Oh my God, I can't even
believe you said that.

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:31.157
Me and my sister are obsessed!

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.660
Do you actually know
how to do stained glass?

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.493
- Yeah.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.350
- My sister and I are obsessed

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.963
with learning how to do stained
glass. This is a real thing.

00:01:35.963 --> 00:01:36.800
- I can teach you.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.633
- I-

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:38.950
- Well, no, forgotten that.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.783
- I want to learn! Do a YouTube special.

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.140
Yeah, I'm like do
something, we wanna learn.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.560
That's a random thing anyway.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.712
- Totally random.

00:01:43.712 --> 00:01:45.951
And I'd been to all these amazing
churches around the world,

00:01:45.951 --> 00:01:46.844
you know, I'd seen all these-

00:01:46.844 --> 00:01:47.677
- They're beautiful.

00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:48.510
- And I thought - what's that?

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.343
- It's beautiful.

00:01:49.343 --> 00:01:50.420
- Yeah. But I thought,
how hard could it be?

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.514
It's already glass, only colored.

00:01:51.514 --> 00:01:52.640
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.107
- They've been doing this for
years. How hard could it be?

00:01:54.107 --> 00:01:55.352
- It was a big deal.

00:01:55.352 --> 00:01:56.390
- These artists and (laughs)

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.040
- So take our little glass
cutter and my soldering iron

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.780
and I started going to stained glass class

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.930
with the thought of
supporting my future family

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.090
as a stained glass master, which...

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.050
thank God that didn't work out.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.840
- It didn't pan out? It didn't pan out.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.687
- So and there was this girl,
it was this burning hot girl.

00:02:10.687 --> 00:02:13.291
And it was just like,
oh my God, I just, I,

00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:15.490
and of course she had a boyfriend.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.323
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:16.323 --> 00:02:17.300
- And she wanted nothing to do with me.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.640
And I would try and, you know,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.430
I was never really good
with chat with girls,

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.164
which is one of the reasons
I picked the guitar up.

00:02:23.164 --> 00:02:25.682
It's 'cuz I was hoping they'd come to me

00:02:25.682 --> 00:02:26.931
- (laughs) This is how
I shall communicate.

00:02:26.931 --> 00:02:28.236
- [Rick] Instead of me
going to them, you know.

00:02:28.236 --> 00:02:29.270
- It was a good idea.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.331
- I mean, you can never
go wrong with the guitar.

00:02:30.331 --> 00:02:31.164
- Yeah.

00:02:31.164 --> 00:02:31.997
- I mean, it's a guitar.

00:02:31.997 --> 00:02:33.438
- I used to carry an empty
case before I learned to play.

00:02:33.438 --> 00:02:35.123
(everyone laughing)

00:02:35.123 --> 00:02:36.183
- You're like Joey from "Friends"

00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:39.150
leaning on the Ferrari or
whatever. That's amazing.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:39.983
- Hi honey, how are you?

00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:41.040
No, I was never that guy really.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.450
I was very shy and I'd say stuff like,

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.800
"Hey, you look really nice today.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.793
You know, are they Jordache
jeans? They're awesome."

00:02:46.793 --> 00:02:47.626
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:47.626 --> 00:02:50.219
And cause it was the '80s.

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:51.729
- Oh my God I love you so much!

00:02:51.729 --> 00:02:52.562
I love it.

00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:54.270
So what were your like '80s jams?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.290
What were you jamming to in the '80s?

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.920
- Well, you know, you can't
be a child of the '80s

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.200
and not love Michael Jackson.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.730
- Oh yes, absolutely. Prince.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:00.563
- [Dulé] Yes.
- Yeah.

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:01.560
- Prince and all that.
- Yeah.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.660
- But I'm from a town
who is of a boyhood home

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.930
of a great rocker.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.220
And you might know this person
if I sing this song to you.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.053
- [Kelly] Okay, go.

00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:11.274
- Shot through the heart.

00:03:11.274 --> 00:03:12.107
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:12.975
- And you're to blame!

00:03:12.975 --> 00:03:14.901
Yes. Jon Bon Jovi's from my hometown.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:15.980
- Okay.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.890
- I actually went to middle school

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.232
with his younger brother Matt.

00:03:18.232 --> 00:03:19.810
- [Kelly] That's so small world!

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.410
- Yeah. Yep! Well, speaking
of the '80s too,

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.420
do you remember when MTV gave
away Bon Jovi's house on MTV?

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.610
Anybody? Anybody? Nobody? Just me?

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.360
- Do you remember when
MTV played music videos?

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.490
- It was at that same time.
It was at that same time!

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.328
- Do y'all remember that?

00:03:32.328 --> 00:03:33.839
- I don't watch TV.

00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:37.980
- I- well, if you watched,
you wouldn't see music videos.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.450
I was like, why do y'all
call this MTV anymore anyway?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.460
It was just weird.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.770
But no, I don't remember that.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:46.220
- Yeah. But, MTV came to my
little town in New Jersey.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.053
It was a huge thing

00:03:47.053 --> 00:03:48.900
cuz they were coming to
give away Bon Jovi's house.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.733
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:50.566
- And they gave away his house

00:03:50.566 --> 00:03:52.300
and that's when Matt moved away.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.442
- Maybe that's when they started.

00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:55.570
Maybe that's when they
started giving away houses

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:56.920
and stopped playing music videos.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.080
- See what I'm saying.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.330
- Anyway, you've got a
big tour this summer.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.163
So are you excited?

00:04:02.163 --> 00:04:03.320
I know every musician's pretty pumped

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.430
about getting back out there right?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.460
- [Rick] Hm.
- Yeah?

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.520
- Yeah, very excited.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.884
We're going out with Men
at Work and John Waite.

00:04:08.884 --> 00:04:09.717
- Yeah!

00:04:09.717 --> 00:04:11.640
- Yeah, Men at Work haven't
been out in a long time,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.110
so it's gonna be, and
they're both great guys.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:17.170
I love both Colin and
John and amazing voices.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.920
And it's gonna be, you
know, wall to wall hits,

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.120
it's gonna be a great show.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:20.953
- I was gonna say.

00:04:20.953 --> 00:04:22.960
- And we're all, you know, I'm
an Aussie, Colin's an Aussie.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.470
Well, he's Scottish, but
he grew up in Australia.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.303
- Yeah.

00:04:26.303 --> 00:04:27.640
- And John Waite got one of my, you know,

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.528
top 10 voices of all time,
rock voices, just incredible

00:04:30.528 --> 00:04:31.850
So it's gonna be a great show.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.540
And they're great guys,
it's gonna be a great hang.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.670
And so we're all looking forward to it.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.640
- Are y'all ever gonna,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.714
cuz this is my favorite
thing that people do

00:04:37.714 --> 00:04:39.370
when they all get on stage

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.770
and you all do something together.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.170
Are you gonna do something together?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.003
- Yeah, yeah, we will.

00:04:43.003 --> 00:04:44.710
We haven't worked it out
yet, but it's, we all-

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:45.950
- [Kelly] Work that out for all of us.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:46.783
- Yes ma'am.

00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:47.830
- Yeah, yeah, okay.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.640
I command it.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.370
Well, tickets for Rick's
2022 tour with Men at Work

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.010
and John Waite are on sale now.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.580
But for everybody in our
audience, it's your lucky day.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.052
'Cuz you're all getting tickets
to Rick's show here in LA!

00:05:01.052 --> 00:05:04.303
(audience cheers)

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.265
You are going too! We're going too.

